{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:58:35.269Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Source change** (`src/cli/lint.ts`):\n- Removed the injectable `exit` option from `LintCommandOptions`.\n- On any invalid linted change, `lintCommand` now throws `new CommandError('', { exitCode: 1 })` after printing the same findings/count/JSON as before; valid runs still return `{ valid, entries }`.\n- Updated the doc comment.\n\n**New test** (`tests/lint-command-error.test.ts`): direct invalid call rejects with an empty `CommandError` (exit 1) and leaves `process.exitCode` unchanged; direct valid call returns its result; through `runCliCaptured`, invalid exits 1 with unchanged stderr findings and no stdout, valid exits 0.\n\n**Converted existing tests** that passed `exit` to `lintCommand` or read its exit code, across `impact-lint`, `lint-findings`, `lint-output`, `lint-repository-count`, `lint-skip-rejected`, `linter`, `proposal-writes-schema`, `validator-missing`, `scope-lint`, `steering-plan`, and `steering-plan-default-branch`. For the two worktree tests, I preserved the folder/finding assertions by parsing the JSON that lint writes before throwing.\n\nVerified:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/lint-command-error.test.ts` — 4/4 pass.\n- All modified test files pass.\n- `pnpm verify` (proposal verify) passes: CLI/UI typechecks, build, full test suite, and `biome check`.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/141-commands-report-failure/.run/results/1.md`. No files changed outside the task scope except that result file. No git commands run."}}
